111 REM CW% IS HOW MANY CHARACTERS ONE CELL TAKES. THE MACHINE BOOTS IN
112 REM 80 COLUMNS, WHERE ONE CELL NEEDS TWO. SWITCH THE TERMINAL TO
113 REM 40X24 WITH THE UST KEY (SYSTEM MENU, "FORMAT EKRANA") AND SET
114 REM CW%=1 - THEN ONE WIDE CHARACTER IS ONE CELL.
115 REM A CELL IS A SQUARE WITH A THICK BORDER, THE WAY THE TETRIS WE
116 REM REMEMBER DREW IT. NO SUCH CHARACTER EXISTS IN THE ROM FONT -
117 REM 160..191 IS ALL LINES AND CORNERS - SO 128, 129 AND 130 ARE
118 REM REDRAWN BEFORE THE RUN BY THE FONT EDITOR OFF THE SYSTEM DISK:
119 REM 128 IS THE LEFT HALF OF THE SQUARE, 129 THE RIGHT HALF, 130 THE
120 REM WHOLE SQUARE FOR THE WIDE FORMAT. ALL THREE HAVE A GLYPH IN THE
121 REM STOCK ROM - ARROWS - SO AN UNPREPARED MACHINE STILL PLAYS.
122 CB$=CHR$(128)+CHR$(129)
